From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ir3: Write zero for undefined phi sources

emit_undef() turns every undefined value into an immediate 0, except
when it is a phi source: read_phi_src() then gives the phi no source on
that edge, and the phi keeps whatever is in its register. Some apps read
uninitialized shader variables and render as intended only if they read
as zero. Xiaomi Weather's sky shader accumulates into an uninitialized
vec3 in a loop, so the undefined initial value reaches the loop phi, and
on Turnip the whole sky turns black.

Write an immediate 0 at the end of the predecessor instead, with the
phi's type and register file, so that phi sources behave like the other
uses of an undefined value. NIR is not changed; only phis with an
undefined source gain a move in that predecessor. Undefined values that
nir_opt_undef has already replaced (with NaN for float-only uses, or by
dropping an undefined bcsel operand) are not affected.

In Settings, the launcher, Etar and Edge (WebGL included) every shader
compiles to the same binary as before. In the weather app one fragment
shader changes, from 82 to 85 instructions, and the sky renders
correctly; with fp16 disabled, a cloud shader that returns before
writing its output no longer shows garbage either.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
index 3d707df..3f75bca 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
@@ -4356,8 +4356,18 @@ read_phi_src(struct ir3_context *ctx, struct ir3_block *blk,
    nir_foreach_phi_src (nsrc, nphi) {
       if (blk->nblock == nsrc->pred) {
          if (nir_src_is_undef(nsrc->src)) {
-            /* Create an ir3 undef */
-            return NULL;
+            /* Write 0 at the end of the predecessor, like emit_undef() does
+             * for every other undefined value. A phi source left undefined
+             * keeps whatever is in the register on this edge, and apps that
+             * read uninitialized variables, or leave a fragment output
+             * unwritten on some path, then get stale values.
+             */
+            type_t type =
+               utype_for_size(ir3_bitsize(ctx, nphi->def.bit_size));
+            struct ir3_builder build =
+               ir3_builder_at(ir3_before_terminator(blk));
+            return create_immed_typed_shared(
+               &build, 0, type, phi->dsts[0]->flags & IR3_REG_SHARED);
          } else {
             /* We need to insert the move at the end of the block */
             struct ir3_block *old_block = ctx->block;
